From: Kernel audit <littleddfu@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sctp: size the ASCONF del-pickup parameter from the pending address

sctp_make_asconf_update_ip() computes the chunk size in a first pass and
fills the chunk in a second.  When asoc->asconf_addr_del_pending is set,
the sizing pass charges the extra DEL_IP parameter using addr_param_len,
which at that point holds the address parameter length of the address
being walked in the caller's array:

	addr_param_len = af->to_addr_param(addr, &addr_param);
	...
	if (asoc->asconf_addr_del_pending && !del_pickup) {
		/* reuse the parameter length from the same scope one */
		totallen += paramlen;
		totallen += addr_param_len;

The fill pass, however, derives the length from asconf_addr_del_pending's
own address family:

	addr = asoc->asconf_addr_del_pending;
	af = sctp_get_af_specific(addr->v4.sin_family);
	addr_param_len = af->to_addr_param(addr, &addr_param);

The comment states an assumption ("the same scope one") that nothing
enforces.  A pending-delete IPv6 address contributes a 20-byte address
parameter while IPv4 additions contribute 8, so the chunk is
under-reserved by 12 bytes and sctp_addto_chunk() writes past the
reservation, tripping skb_over_panic():

  kernel BUG at net/core/skbuff.c:214!
  RIP: 0010:skb_over_panic+0x14f/0x160
  Call Trace:
   skb_put+0x110/0x1f0
   sctp_make_asconf_update_ip+0xb08/0xdb0
   sctp_send_asconf_add_ip+0x85f/0xad0
   sctp_setsockopt+0x778/0xed0
   __x64_sys_setsockopt+0x13f/0x180

The endpoint and association bind lists have to disagree for the
del_pending branch to be armed: sctp_bindx_rem() requires the endpoint to
hold at least two addresses, while the branch requires the association to
hold exactly the one being removed.  Address scoping provides that -
sctp_in_scope() only copies an endpoint address into a new association
when addr_scope <= peer_scope, so associating with a global-scope peer
leaves private IPv4 addresses on the endpoint but out of the association.
The result is reachable by an unprivileged process in a user+net
namespace using only setsockopt(SCTP_SOCKOPT_BINDX_REM/ADD).

Derive the reservation from the pending address itself.

diff --git a/net/sctp/sm_make_chunk.c b/net/sctp/sm_make_chunk.c
index e25612e9d082..e96844b5a56d 100644
--- a/net/sctp/sm_make_chunk.c
+++ b/net/sctp/sm_make_chunk.c
@@ -2850,7 +2850,7 @@ struct sctp_chunk *sctp_make_asconf_update_ip(struct sctp_association *asoc,
 					      struct sockaddr *addrs,
 					      int addrcnt, __be16 flags)
 {
-	union sctp_addr_param addr_param;
+	union sctp_addr_param addr_param, del_addr_param;
 	struct sctp_addip_param	param;
 	int paramlen = sizeof(param);
 	struct sctp_chunk *retval;
@@ -2858,7 +2858,7 @@ struct sctp_chunk *sctp_make_asconf_update_ip(struct sctp_association *asoc,
 	union sctp_addr *addr;
 	int totallen = 0, i;
 	int del_pickup = 0;
-	struct sctp_af *af;
+	struct sctp_af *af, *del_af;
 	void *addr_buf;
 
 	/* Get total length of all the address parameters. */
@@ -2873,9 +2873,23 @@ struct sctp_chunk *sctp_make_asconf_update_ip(struct sctp_association *asoc,
 
 		addr_buf += af->sockaddr_len;
 		if (asoc->asconf_addr_del_pending && !del_pickup) {
-			/* reuse the parameter length from the same scope one */
+			/* The pending delete address is not necessarily of the
+			 * same family as the addresses being added, so its
+			 * address parameter length must be derived from the
+			 * pending address itself.  Reusing addr_param_len here
+			 * under-reserves the chunk by 12 bytes whenever a v6
+			 * delete is picked up alongside v4 additions, and the
+			 * fill pass below then writes past the reservation.
+			 */
+			del_af = sctp_get_af_specific(
+				asoc->asconf_addr_del_pending->v4.sin_family);
+			if (!del_af)
+				return NULL;
+
 			totallen += paramlen;
-			totallen += addr_param_len;
+			totallen += del_af->to_addr_param(
+					asoc->asconf_addr_del_pending,
+					&del_addr_param);
 			del_pickup = 1;
 
 			pr_debug("%s: picked same-scope del_pending addr, "
